---
title: "get_daily_attendance_counts_for_month (Attendance Summary Functions)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_validate: receive(start_date, end_date)
    q_validate --> q_filter: SELECT from attendance.attendances
    q_filter --> q_check_range: a.date >= start_date AND a.date <= end_date
    q_check_range --> q_check_type: range condition met
    q_check_type --> q_group: a.type = 'in'
    q_check_type --> q_filter: a.type != 'in' (skip row)
    q_check_range --> q_filter: outside range (skip row)
    q_group --> q_count: GROUP BY a.date
    q_count --> q_order: COUNT(DISTINCT a.user_id)
    q_order --> [*]: ORDER BY a.date, return (date, count) rows

    note right of q_check_range
        INV-001: Only rows where a.date is within [start_date, end_date] are included
        INV-002: Only 'in' type attendance records are counted
    end note

    note right of q_count
        INV-003: Each user_id is counted at most once per date (DISTINCT)
        INV-004: Result is ordered ascending by date
    end note
